{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/487155-are-there-6-dots-disciplines-ranks","id":487155,"title":"Are there 6+ dots disciplines ranks?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-21T03:58:26-07:00","id":487155,"title":"Are there 6+ dots disciplines ranks?","content":"OK, <i>now </i>I sound like a total newbie. So, in yet another if-it-exists-in-VtM-does-it-in-VtR, are there 6+ dots Disciplines, stuff that you could only unlock with very high blood potency, or that elder vampires would be known to have and would drive fear in the heart of players? If so, in what book, because I haven't seen it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T04:08:54-07:00","id":487174,"title":"","content":"No 6+ dots disciplines are currently available for nWOD Vampire 2e. These unique powers are usually represented by various Devotions.<br /> <br /> However, it's possible that 6+ Disciplines may become available in the release of VtR: A Thousand Years of Night, the V:tR sourcebook for elders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T04:17:35-07:00","id":487180,"title":"","content":"It's very unlikely. It has been kinda confirmed by the developers and by the 2e corebook itself that disciplines only go up to 5. (the old corebook had the possibility at Bloodpotency 6+, new corebook does not). <br /> <br /> However, as branford mentioned, the thematic thing is still in the game. Really, what's the difference between a Discipline at 6 and a really powerful devotion? From mechanical standpoint, a little bit... from narrative and driving of fear into hearts of players standpoint? None at all. So take those mega devotions and bring ruin to the neonates who can't use them. (Since they mostly have a big blood cost, and even if a Neonate decides to learn it.. it's no gonna be as awesome, just because of how many turns he'll need to unleash it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T05:17:39-07:00","id":487191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/487155-are-there-6-dots-disciplines-ranks?p=487180#post487180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's very unlikely. It has been kinda confirmed by the developers and by the 2e corebook itself that disciplines only go up to 5. (the old corebook had the possibility at Bloodpotency 6+, new corebook does not).</div> </div> </div> </div>No 6+ disciplines powers by the 2e corebook? Do you mean Blood &amp; Smoke? Can you reference a page or something? <b>That</b> would be nice to know indeed.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T05:45:13-07:00","id":487204,"title":"","content":"I think the general idea in second edition is that any of those elder tricks from masquerade can be replicated with five or less dots in appropriate disciplines, so a sixth+ dot in a discipline isn't really needed. <br /> <br /> Plus even an elder can end up with low blood potency thanks to torpor, so it makes sense that they would develop their powers in a manner that didn't rely on being at the peak of efficiency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T06:01:18-07:00","id":487211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/487155-are-there-6-dots-disciplines-ranks?p=487191#post487191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No 6+ disciplines powers by the 2e corebook? Do you mean Blood &amp; Smoke? Can you reference a page or something? <b>That</b> would be nice to know indeed.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, 2e corebook is Blood &amp; Smoke. Can't get a page reference at the moment, but just open up the part where it describes the benefits of Blood Potency above 6+. In the previous Corebook it said that you can increase your Skills, Attributes AND disciplines above 5 with high blood potency. Now it's excluding the Disciplines part. <br /> This has been mentioned before hand on these forums and MachineIV confirmed that that's the intent <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T06:31:37-07:00","id":487215,"title":"","content":"I guess maybe you could justify letting the physical disciplines go up to ten, because they're pretty straightforward. So long as you're ok with elders that can punch a neonate in half.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T06:42:20-07:00","id":487218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/487155-are-there-6-dots-disciplines-ranks?p=487191#post487191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No 6+ disciplines powers by the 2e corebook? Do you mean Blood &amp; Smoke? Can you reference a page or something? <b>That</b> would be nice to know indeed.</div> </div> </div> </div>On p155, 'Coils, like Disciplines, are on a ladder from one to five dots.'<br /> <br /> In addition to Devotions taking the place of 6+ dot Disciplines, in first edition there were Disciplines and Devotions that had a high Blood Potency prerequisite.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T19:32:48-07:00","id":487859,"title":"","content":"As far as Masquerade to Requiem, the 5th dot of a Discipline in 2.0 is a 5-7 dot equivalent in Masquerade. As said, there won't be anything official greater than 5 dots, but any power is still possible so if you were converting it would become a Devotion. Blood Potency is more fluid than Generation so it makes a poor requirement, generally speaking beyond a few dots. Age is too arbitrary so it can get a bit difficult when coming up with Elder only powers. You'll have to wait for Thousand Years of Night to see how they go about it. In 1.0 there was a few bits like that written for specific characters scattered about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T02:06:25-07:00","id":488085,"title":"","content":"The solution we got in the current core book is great one. If a discipline costs 7+ vitae to enact, in mostly everbodies eyes it's gonna be an Elder only thing, because a neonate would get use out of it far too rarely for it to be worth it. <br /> Just look at the invincibility one... a neonate can become immune to harm every 5 turns? Wow... An elder can be invincible for several turns in a row tho, that sounds much much better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T07:32:55-07:00","id":488263,"title":"","content":"There will be an Elder's book(A Thousand Years of Night), maybe this kind of thing will be talked there?<br /> Either as 6+ powers or devotions with Blood Potency requirements?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4055,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","user":"Felipe","date":". 04-22-2015, 10:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T08:31:13-07:00","id":488291,"title":"","content":"It will likely just be <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/402794-are-physical-disciplines-uncapped?p=404124#post404124\">devotions</a>.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T10:47:08-07:00","id":488473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/487155-are-there-6-dots-disciplines-ranks?p=487218#post487218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On p155, 'Coils, like Disciplines, are on a ladder from one to five dots.'<br /> <br /> In addition to Devotions taking the place of 6+ dot Disciplines, in first edition there were Disciplines and Devotions that had a high Blood Potency prerequisite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense, just have to check 1e doesn't say something similar to make things dubious - but thanks anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T11:17:31-07:00","id":488513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/487155-are-there-6-dots-disciplines-ranks?p=488291#post488291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It will likely just be <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/402794-are-physical-disciplines-uncapped?p=404124#post404124\">devotions</a>.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thought it makes you wonder about single-discipline devotions, doesn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T11:26:36-07:00","id":488533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/487155-are-there-6-dots-disciplines-ranks?p=488513#post488513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thought it makes you wonder about single-discipline devotions, doesn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, what about Theban Sorcery and Cruac beyond the five dots?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T11:31:08-07:00","id":488536,"title":"","content":"The single discipline devotions seen so far have all been first edition discipline powers that got replaced in 2e. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T14:17:08-07:00","id":488706,"title":"","content":"There really hasn't been much follow up to how powerful elders get with disciplines past rank 5. If I'm remembering right, the only groups that had any follow up to 6+ was Mages and Changelings. I wouldn't count on anything coming out or it if does it will probably be a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1279-badger-king","name":"Badger King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1279_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T16:25:45-07:00","id":488816,"title":"","content":"I feel the disciplines have a thematic progression that naturally stops at the fifth dot. Let's say Auspex, which is about insight/empathy. First you have insight into/empathy with people, then empathy with objects, which is naturally more difficult. At the fourth dot you have near perfect empathy with another living being, and at the fifth your insight is no longer bound to your physical body. Going further than this would be transcendence or Buddha-like enlightenment, which I don't think would suit Vampire, the theme has gone as far as possible while still feeling Vampiric.<br /> <br /> Progression now, would involve mixing themes or focusing aspects of them, which is the ground devotions cover.<br /> <br /> (I don't have the core with me, as usual, so I hope I didn't arse up Auspex!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T16:33:05-07:00","id":488819,"title":"","content":"Since this is like the third thread we've had asking if disciplines go past 5 and when we're getting disciplines past 5 and based on some of the posts in these threads I get the feeling people really want disciplines or abilities that go past 5.<br /> <br /> So I have to ask, why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T16:59:54-07:00","id":488844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/487155-are-there-6-dots-disciplines-ranks?p=488819#post488819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since this is like the third thread we've had asking if disciplines go past 5 and when we're getting disciplines past 5 and based on some of the posts in these threads I get the feeling people really want disciplines or abilities that go past 5.<br /> <br /> So I have to ask, why?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is just a Masquerade phantom pain. People feel the need to make old Vampires more powerful by enhance they Disciplines. But the 2ed Way to handle that is, that the Disciplines are just the Vampire default-powers. The interesting things are the devotions. Might comes from the Techniques you learn. The unique way you train and handle the beast. There is no need for Disciplines above 5 and I will be confused if they ever appear in a 2Ed. Book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T17:19:26-07:00","id":488855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sethos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/487155-are-there-6-dots-disciplines-ranks?p=488844#post488844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it is just a Masquerade phantom pain.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And I think this is an arrogant assumption.<br /> <br /> I like long term games.after a point, skills and attributes aren't that interesting, and I don't want to get EVERY discipline. Now, I don't mind the elder devotion path, though i preferred the older &quot;Unique&quot; concept. I'd have liked a &quot;Build a discipline&quot; system ala Blood Sorcery, but with a more ramped up scale.This was only compounded when Ancient Mysteries was unimpressive, followed by the Archmage book.<br /> <br /> I enjoy high end games, but Mage isn't my thing. I like vampire. I like the concept of methuselahs being different. I liked the concept of taking political power in the setting, not because of alliances, but because of what you can PERSONALLY do if someone opposes it.<br /> <br /> Everytime this topic comes up, I want to ask, Why not? Why are so many insistent on limiting player options in this regard? I get it, you like street level games. That doesn't mean you should lobby against people who enjoy more higher tiered gameplay, or long running games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T17:43:53-07:00","id":488876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/487155-are-there-6-dots-disciplines-ranks?p=488855#post488855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I get it, you like street level games. That doesn't mean you should lobby against people who enjoy more higher tiered gameplay, or long running games.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I think this is an arrogant assumption as well.<br /> <br /> First of all, don't be upset just because I offer my estimations. I feel the topic of this thread is rather emotionally charged. Let us all calm down.<br /> <br /> Street level is not my intention. I am a fan of a vast range of power levels who act together and against each other. All I whanted to say is, that there is no need for Disciplines above 5 to create relay powerful characters. Create a Daeva with Vigor 5 and Majesty 5. Then gave him a Devotion which brings that two together and you have a one man natural force.<br /> <br /> Gave a Nosfearatu Obfuscate and Nightmare at 5 and a Devotion playing with that two and he can shift the world like a Demigod. Bring Vigor into play, to make the shifts permanent and physical and he can create his own reality like a God.<br /> <br /> Take a Mekhet with a Obfuscate 5 and Celerity 5 Devotion. He could be as close to teleportation as you can get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T17:49:16-07:00","id":488881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/487155-are-there-6-dots-disciplines-ranks?p=488855#post488855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everytime this topic comes up, I want to ask, Why not? Why are so many insistent on limiting player options in this regard? I get it, you like street level games. That doesn't mean you should lobby against people who enjoy more higher tiered gameplay, or long running games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't like street level games any more than others, and I certainly don't lobby against other people wanting different tiered gameplay.<br /> <br /> But I really don't think you need range 6-10 powers to make that happen. As it is, blood sorcery is incredibly powerful, and even without it you have devotions like Dark Decree, which is probably one of the most powerful abilities in all of World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://i.warosu.org/data/tg/img/0348/09/1410567382296.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-22-2015, 09:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T17:56:18-07:00","id":488887,"title":"","content":"So, if you do have a devotion with a blood potency requirement, what does that do to the experience cost? <br /> <br /> I mean if you go for a single discipline one, make it bp 6+ and price it at 3xp that's effectively the same as the sixth dot. Especially if you toss in a &quot;+1 to [discipline] rolls&quot; as a side benefit. <br /> <br /> Then do something similar at 7, 8, 9, and 10. Voilla. You have hacked in elder disciplines without actually changing the system at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T17:59:30-07:00","id":488890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/487155-are-there-6-dots-disciplines-ranks?p=488881#post488881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't like street level games any more than others, and I certainly don't lobby against other people wanting different tiered gameplay.<br /> <br /> But I really don't think you need range 6-10 powers to make that happen. As it is, blood sorcery is incredibly powerful, and even without it you have devotions like Dark Decree, which is probably one of the most powerful abilities in all of World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't speak for the rest, but this is why, even though I don't mind if we don't get them, it is that one feature I would be looking forward to most excitedly:<ul><li>Crossover all the way into Cosmic Tier. Why? Because the point of nWoD was to provide tools, and I have something to do with said tools but said tools are not available. Already had two games which involved a Mage, a Lupine and two Kindred, that we wanted to take cosmic near the (premature) end. We would've had much more fun with it.</li> <li>Room to go up in chronicles that span the millennia.</li> <li>If you don't mind devotions powerful enough as 6+ disciplines, I don't get why we shouldn't name them as such, other than Metamphiesophobia (fear of Masquerade)? I like to keep things simple and the simplest thing for higher powers is adding an extra dot to the right of the fifth one. That's why we also don't use social combat rules or conditions (except as flaws and derangements) around my table.</li> </ul>I can think of more reasons, but I would just be lobbying for 6+ powers since only the three above interest me. Just as Strange, Dead Love did not turn Requiem into a romantic gothic game, I don't see the reason why we need to go explicitly out of our way to ask that a tool for a toolbox system is never provided to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T18:02:56-07:00","id":488894,"title":"","content":"We could come up with a Lexicon just for the terms the community uses to piss off one another (always in good spirit and with no ill intentions)... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T18:07:07-07:00","id":488898,"title":"","content":"I think the difference between 5+ Disciplines and Devotions is that considering the cheap price of Disciplines, your Neonate is 9 Experience into the game and is now on their 6th dot in a discipline. 9 more Experience and they're wielding cosmic tier power. At least with something like Dark Decree you have to have some story to it where you've taken blood from someone outside of your clan to get access to their disciplines, and are spending out of clan discipline costs, which admittedly aren't much more expensive, but you can tack on a Blood Potency prerequisite.<br /> <br /> And that's not even taking into account my belief that the disciplines are very complete, considering what they can do. Dominate is practically mastered at the third dot, what should an 8th dot do that a 5th couldn't?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T18:10:05-07:00","id":488899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sethos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/487155-are-there-6-dots-disciplines-ranks?p=488876#post488876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I think this is an arrogant assumption as well.<br /> <br /> First of all, don't be upset just because I offer my estimations. I feel the topic of this thread is rather emotionally charged. Let us all calm down.<br /> <br /> Street level is not my intention. I am a fan of a vast range of power levels who act together and against each other. All I whanted to say is, that there is no need for Disciplines above 5 to create relay powerful characters. Create a Daeva with Vigor 5 and Majesty 5. Then gave him a Devotion which brings that two together and you have a one man natural force.<br /> <br /> Gave a Nosfearatu Obfuscate and Nightmare at 5 and a Devotion playing with that two and he can shift the world like a Demigod. Bring Vigor into play, to make the shifts permanent and physical and he can create his own reality like a God.<br /> <br /> Take a Mekhet with a Obfuscate 5 and Celerity 5 Devotion. He could be as close to teleportation as you can get.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't referring to you specifically. I was talking in regard to the way it has come up quite a few times on forums. People always rail against there ever being a high level book or codified rules for methuselah for precisely the reasons I mentioned. So many options for standard, day to day games, but people always come in insisting that there be no 6+ advancement, either through devotions or disciplines.<br /> <br /> There is always some sort of panic attack people get when it comes up in regard to Requiem for some unfathomable reason. Like it will force a higher tier game or something on those that prefer to keep lower tier.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T18:20:12-07:00","id":488905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/487155-are-there-6-dots-disciplines-ranks?p=488899#post488899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is always some sort of panic attack people get when it comes up in regard to Requiem for some unfathomable reason. Like it will force a higher tier game or something on those that prefer to keep lower tier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh that, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/64679-elder-book-anounced\">yeah I've seen that</a>. That actually seems to be more from people who don't like Masquerade, or something. They always end up comparing it to the Jyhad or some other Masquerade thing. I want ancient powerful vampires, and it would be awesome to be able to play one. I've said as such before. I just don't think 6-10 Dots are necessary for it, and it can be better done in other ways, like tying devotions to Blood Potency.<br /> <br /> I hope El Abominar still exists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T18:38:30-07:00","id":488917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/487155-are-there-6-dots-disciplines-ranks?p=488898#post488898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the difference between 5+ Disciplines and Devotions is that considering the cheap price of Disciplines, your Neonate is 9 Experience into the game and is now on their 6th dot in a discipline. 9 more Experience and they're wielding cosmic tier power. At least with something like Dark Decree you have to have some story to it where you've taken blood from someone outside of your clan to get access to their disciplines, and are spending out of clan discipline costs, which admittedly aren't much more expensive, but you can tack on a Blood Potency prerequisite.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it is the XP- price. At least not for me. I have no real interest in xp costs. But I think you are right if you say...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/487155-are-there-6-dots-disciplines-ranks?p=488898#post488898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's not even taking into account my belief that the disciplines are very complete, considering what they can do. Dominate is practically mastered at the third dot, what should an 8th dot do that a 5th couldn't?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is imho. the concept of how Vampires and they Powers work. I think, the Disciplines are powerful but limited in what they can do. Because the beast is limited. If you read Blood an Smoke / Vampire 2 Ed. You probably noticed that every Discipline is connected to the Beast. If you go to far above the highest level, discipline would lose they themes and start to become something more Magic like.<br /> But the creativity of the human part of a Vampire is endless. He can connect every aspect of his Beast to unleash powerful reactions, like an chemist who mixes Nitroglycerin.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure we will get mighty powers for ancient Characters, but I'm pretty sure they will com as devotions, not as high level disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T18:51:33-07:00","id":488945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BarbeChenue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/487155-are-there-6-dots-disciplines-ranks#post487155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, <i>now </i>I sound like a total newbie. So, in yet another if-it-exists-in-VtM-does-it-in-VtR, are there 6+ dots Disciplines, stuff that you could only unlock with very high blood potency, or that elder vampires would be known to have and would drive fear in the heart of players? If so, in what book, because I haven't seen it...</div> </div> </div> </div>A ffffffew are scattered in some of the1st edition books.<br /> Hooowever consensus seems to be that that is not the way to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T22:25:19-07:00","id":489066,"title":"","content":"What happened to <i>A Thousand Years of Night</i>, BTW? I couldn't find any recent news about it. Sounds like a delightful idea of a book, and a lot more interesting than my initial expectation of &quot;elder powers&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T23:30:22-07:00","id":489102,"title":"","content":"They're working on Secrets of the Covenants at the moment, and it's still in first draft so we've got a ways to go before we see a Thousand Years of Night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T00:39:23-07:00","id":489136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/487155-are-there-6-dots-disciplines-ranks?p=488899#post488899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wasn't referring to you specifically. I was talking in regard to the way it has come up quite a few times on forums. People always rail against there ever being a high level book or codified rules for methuselah for precisely the reasons I mentioned. So many options for standard, day to day games, but people always come in insisting that there be no 6+ advancement, either through devotions or disciplines.<br /> <br /> There is always some sort of panic attack people get when it comes up in regard to Requiem for some unfathomable reason. Like it will force a higher tier game or something on those that prefer to keep lower tier.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, I specifically rail against those options not because I'm against them existing. But because I know that these high tiered things are eating up the space of things which could be more widely used by the player community. I do think that those cosmic games are quite rare, and as such any content made for them will be largely useless to others. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T02:19:18-07:00","id":489185,"title":"","content":"I only rail against 6+ disciplines. I think it is a poor implementation for higher level games, specifically because of how it was done in Masquerade. I think a 5 dot devotion, possibly with multiple Disciplines, is a better way to go. I think they can cover unique powers. I just don't see how the current Disciplines can be extended without each power being unique to a character and that is the realm of Devotions. I do agree that some space should be devoted to designing Devotions when an appropriate home can be found. Requiem has a formula for Disciplines now and I appreciate that greatly. Before I thought some Disciplines were weak and others too strong, based entirely on relative strengths. Maybe I lack imagination but I think combining the power of a couple of 5 dot Disciplines should do anything a vampire should be able to do. Devotions take care of the niche filled by Masquerade's 6+ Disciplines. Now we just need a bit more on how to go about designing Devotions to do what they are supposed to do. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T03:04:50-07:00","id":489197,"title":"","content":"Consider:<br /> <br /> The B&amp;S book is standalone, no other rules or books are needed (or intended) to be able to play games of VtR<br /> <br /> The B&amp;S book does not mention Disciplines above 5 dots<br /> <br /> You are a new player to Vampire<br /> <br /> What part of the game suggests you can have Disciplines of 6 dots?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T04:37:37-07:00","id":489286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/487155-are-there-6-dots-disciplines-ranks?p=489197#post489197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consider:<br /> <br /> The B&amp;S book is standalone, no other rules or books are needed (or intended) to be able to play games of VtR<br /> <br /> The B&amp;S book does not mention Disciplines above 5 dots<br /> <br /> You are a new player to Vampire<br /> <br /> What part of the game suggests you can have Disciplines of 6 dots?</div> </div> </div> </div>The book also provides several examples of &quot;OMFG HOW POWERFUL&quot; devotions (I'm looking at you, Vermin Flood,Riot , Juggernaut's Gait, Force of Nature, Cult of Personality, and to a lesser extend The Wish). <br /> <br /> These are the effects so powerful that they are only gonna be used by elders most of the time (paying the Vitae price is too big for neonates in most cases). So can anyone tell me, what does disciplines at 6+ provide what these Devotions do not provide? A bigger dice pool to your base powers since your discipline score is higher? That's the only thing I can figure out and it's unnecessary in my opinion. You want more dice - improve the base stats (which go above 5)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}